				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove pervasive leading empty lines across Source\n\nStrip the redundant single empty line immediately following the module doc comment in over 400 Rust source files. This includes the Air integration client, ApplicationState persistence and recovery layers, Binary entry points (DNS, TLS, PostHog), Cache subsystems, Command handlers, IPC bridges (Vine, WindServiceAdapters, StatusReporter), RPC services (Cocoon, Echo, Workspace), and Runtime shutdown logic.\n\nThe change consolidates the pattern where `//! ...` comments are followed by a blank line before the first `use` or `struct` declaration, enforcing a tighter, more consistent file header style. No logic, types, or public APIs are modified; the diff is purely cosmetic whitespace normalization.\n\nThis unifies the formatting style across the Mountain codebase, removing stylistic noise from reviews and ensuring the file structure remains uniform regardless of the specific module or feature.\n\nRefs #CLAUDE.md",
			"SHA": "58c1911fec75324953e6b953ff369ea99ef4bcf4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T02:56:58Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove pervasive `non_snake_case` allowance across Source\n\nStrip the `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` crate-level attribute from over 300 modules spanning Air integration, ApplicationState, Binary entry points, caching layers, command surfaces, environment providers, IPC handlers, RPC services, telemetry, and runtime logic. This aligns the Rust codebase with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention enforced by CLAUDE.md.\n\nThe change eliminates suppression of warnings for module and struct names like `AirMetrics`, `DnsHealthStatus`, and `MountainProvideDefinition`, which already follow the required casing. Additionally, clean up `mod.rs` documentation paths to use `self::` syntax for clarity and remove redundant `unused_variables` and `dead_code` allowances where they were bundled with the removed attribute.\n\nThis unifies the codebase stylistically, ensuring that no lints are silently ignored and that future additions must adhere to the standard naming rules.\n\nRefs #CLAUDE.md",
			"SHA": "8b59201f92f79f4090ab5637eb03ae61fed9ed53"
		},
